{
  "id": "grammar.a2.17.02.indefinido",
  "title": "Pretérito Indefinido Review",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Use the pretérito indefinido for completed past events, especially when the time period is finished or a completed event is located in the past. Common forms include aprendí, terminó, recordamos and hicieron."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Aprendí mucho en el curso.",
          "english": "I learned a lot in the course."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "La clase terminó ayer.",
          "english": "The class finished yesterday."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Recordamos la primera lección.",
          "english": "We remembered the first lesson."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Hicieron una foto.",
          "english": "They took a photo."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "aprendí",
          "I learned"
        ],
        [
          "terminó",
          "finished"
        ],
        [
          "recordamos",
          "we remembered"
        ],
        [
          "hicieron",
          "they did / made"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Check the time frame before choosing the tense. A period connected to the present often uses the pretérito perfecto; a finished past period or completed event often uses the indefinido."
    },
    {
      "type": "external-link",
      "topic": "the pretérito perfecto",
